  = note: `for<'x> fn(gdp::Named<'x, fixture::UserId>, gdp::Named<'x, fixture::ProjectId>) {body}` must implement `FnOnce<(gdp::Named<'0, fixture::UserId>, gdp::Named<'1, fixture::ProjectId>)>`, for any two lifetimes `'0` and `'1`...
  = note: ...but it actually implements `FnOnce<(gdp::Named<'2, fixture::UserId>, gdp::Named<'2, fixture::ProjectId>)>`, for some specific lifetime `'2`
